{
  "rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 5–10 days show a sustained rise, the model systematically forecasts too flat/low. Apply an additive uplift that grows with horizon (small at days 1–3, large by days 10–30).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: errors increase with lead time; near-term (1–3d) is close, but 5–30d is materially below realized levels. Use a ramping correction (e.g., linear increase in uplift with forecast day).",
    "Regime shift/structural break lag: after a breakout above the recent 30d range, the model anchors to the old range and fails to rebase. If price exceeds recent 20–30d high, shift the whole forecast path upward (level reset) rather than expecting mean reversion.",
    "Underestimation of volatility and momentum: true outcomes accelerate upward while forecasts remain smooth. Add a momentum term proportional to recent slope/returns, especially for days 5–15 where the miss is largest.",
    "False mean-reversion signal: the model often predicts pullbacks/sideways action after modest dips, but realized prices continue trending up. Suppress mean-reversion adjustments when medium-term momentum (e.g., 10d return) is positive and rising."
  ]
}
